  "record_bodies_before": {
    "courier-relay/protocol-contracts": "Courier Relay delivery-receipt protocols (main.py count/summary/accepted). Current protocol is \"2\" as of trial-ag7: the provider permanently adopted protocol 2 and the integration owner approved making it current, so an omitted \"protocol\" selects \"2\". Protocol \"1\" remains supported when named explicitly.\n\nProtocol 2 contract (as supplied in trial-ag7): the pair (account_id, delivery_id) identifies a delivery; the same delivery_id under a different account identifies a separate delivery. Exactly one receipt is accepted per delivery identity. Accept the receipt with the latest occurred_at UTC instant; equal instants use the smallest record_id (Unicode code-point order). All other receipts for that identity are duplicates. Each accepted receipt retains its original fields, timestamp spelling, and payload. Accepted receipts are presented in original input order. This identity contract comes from the provider's delivery-ID allocation guarantee; account attribution alone does not change that guarantee. It applies to the entire supplied receipt set regardless of receipt dates.\n\nProtocol 1 contract (unchanged, still the applicable rules for explicit \"protocol\":\"1\"): bundled verbatim in vendor/protocol-1.md — delivery_id alone identifies a delivery across all accounts, and the earliest occurred_at UTC instant wins with equal instants using the smallest record_id.\n\nCommands and the versions they serve: count is the single-account command and summary the cross-account batch command; both exist in protocol 1 and 2 and use the selected protocol's identity and selection rules, reporting the protocol actually used. accepted was added in trial-0uv for the current protocol only: request {\"command\":\"accepted\",\"receipts\":[...]} with optional \"protocol\":\"2\", response exactly protocol, accepted_count, duplicate_count, receipts. Its counts equal summary's for the same request, and receipts holds the accepted representatives unchanged in original input order. trial-0uv specified accepted only for the current protocol and did not state behavior for \"protocol\":\"1\"; the implementation therefore answers {\"error\":\"unsupported_protocol\"} for accepted with any protocol other than \"2\" (an implementation choice made in trial-0uv, not a supplied provider rule).\n\nImplementation: main.py maps each version in PROTOCOLS to (identity, rank) functions, and rank_2 negates epoch seconds so the smallest rank still wins; accepted_receipts() returns the winning receipts in input order and backs both counts() and accepted(). SUPPORTED maps each command to the protocol versions it serves."
  },
  "record_bodies_after": {
    "courier-relay/protocol-contracts": "Courier Relay delivery-receipt protocols (main.py count/summary/accepted). Current protocol is \"2\" as of trial-ag7: the provider permanently adopted protocol 2 and the integration owner approved making it current, so an omitted \"protocol\" selects \"2\". Protocol \"1\" remains supported when named explicitly.\n\nProtocol 2 contract (as supplied in trial-ag7): the pair (account_id, delivery_id) identifies a delivery; the same delivery_id under a different account identifies a separate delivery. Exactly one receipt is accepted per delivery identity. Accept the receipt with the latest occurred_at UTC instant; equal instants use the smallest record_id (Unicode code-point order). All other receipts for that identity are duplicates. Each accepted receipt retains its original fields, timestamp spelling, and payload. Accepted receipts are presented in original input order. This identity contract comes from the provider's delivery-ID allocation guarantee; account attribution alone does not change that guarantee. It applies to the entire supplied receipt set regardless of receipt dates.\n\nProtocol 1 contract (unchanged, still the applicable rules for explicit \"protocol\":\"1\"): bundled verbatim in vendor/protocol-1.md — delivery_id alone identifies a delivery across all accounts, and the earliest occurred_at UTC instant wins with equal instants using the smallest record_id. Like protocol 2 it accepts exactly one receipt per identity, returns accepted receipts unchanged (fields, timestamp spelling, payload), and presents them in original input order.\n\nCommands and the versions they serve: count is the single-account command and summary the cross-account batch command; both exist in protocol 1 and 2 and use the selected protocol's identity and selection rules, reporting the protocol actually used. accepted was added in trial-0uv for the current protocol only: request {\"command\":\"accepted\",\"receipts\":[...]} with optional \"protocol\", response exactly protocol, accepted_count, duplicate_count, receipts. Its counts equal summary's for the same request, and receipts holds the accepted representatives unchanged in original input order. trial-vbo permanently extended accepted to explicit \"protocol\":\"1\" for an integration partner, applying the vendor/protocol-1.md identity and representative-selection rules with the same response shape; this supersedes trial-0uv's protocol-2-only limit, so accepted no longer answers {\"error\":\"unsupported_protocol\"} for \"1\". count, summary, and accepted all now serve {\"1\",\"2\"} and still answer {\"error\":\"unsupported_protocol\"} for any other version; unknown commands still answer {\"error\":\"unknown_command\"} and ping still answers {\"status\":\"ok\",\"product\":\"Courier Relay\"}.\n\nImplementation: main.py maps each version in PROTOCOLS to (identity, rank) functions, and rank_2 negates epoch seconds so the smallest rank still wins; accepted_receipts() returns the winning receipts in input order and backs both counts() and accepted(). SUPPORTED maps each command to the protocol versions it serves, which is the only place accepted's version support is declared."
  },
